# Example host configuration. Copy to `.env`, then `pnpm start`
# (or `pnpm dev:host` if the app bundle is already built).
#
# The host (`pnpm dev:host`) serves THREE self-owned modules at once:
#   articles    tool-codegen example — own tools + a generated typed client
#               (typed step callTool + typed widget hooks)
#   tasks       registers its own tools + widget (createToolRegistrar)
#   orders      eager dashboard + a two-step pipeline
#
# All modules are local plugins compiled into the host: they need no other
# server and no env — they run automatically.
#
# The two standalone UI demos need NO env and no server:
#   pnpm dev:widget-playground   isolated widget development (fixture data)
#   pnpm dev:host-portability    one widget under mcp-use / ChatGPT / standalone

# --- Host server (pnpm dev:host) ---
PORT=3010
MCP_URL=http://localhost:3010

# --- articles codegen source (pnpm dev:codegen-source) ---
# Build-time only: the standalone MCP endpoint `pnpm generate` /
# `pnpm generate:check` snapshot to (re)generate the typed articles client.
# Not needed to RUN the host — the host serves the articles tools itself.
ARTICLES_CODEGEN_SOURCE_PORT=4000
ARTICLES_CODEGEN_SOURCE_URL=http://localhost:4000/mcp
